    "type": "string"
   },
   "description": "Material questions the available evidence cannot answer."
  },
  "recommended_action": {
   "type": "string",
   "enum": [
    "close",
    "escalate",
    "collect_more"
   ]
  },
  "additional_evidence_needed": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  }
 }
}

attempts.answer:
{
  "assessment": "malicious",
  "confidence": 0.78,
  "supporting_observations": [
    {
      "claim": "At 13:38 UTC, Dana's workstation recorded a network logon for kim.ortega from WS-KORTEGA-01; shortly afterward, PowerShell ran the documented monthly patch script under kim.ortega's account.",
      "claim_type": "observed_fact",
      "record_ids": ["S07-00077", "S07-00107", "S07-00108"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The PowerShell process launched wusa.exe to install a Windows update, and the proxy recorded Windows Update traffic at the same time. This supports a benign explanation for the reported PowerShell window, considered on its own.",
      "claim_type": "inferred_claim",
      "record_ids": ["S07-00111", "S07-00115", "S07-00116"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "At 14:15 UTC, the domain controller recorded Dana's account requesting a ticket for WS-KORTEGA-01 from 10.20.20.30, and WS-KORTEGA-01 recorded a successful network logon for Dana from that same address. The supplied environment context identifies 10.20.20.30 as the proxy and says remote administration is only performed from WS-KORTEGA-01 inside the office; this activity is inconsistent with that practice and supports an unauthorized-access finding.",
      "claim_type": "inferred_claim",
      "record_ids": ["S07-00262", "S07-00263", "S07-00264"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Sysmon records Google Drive File Stream and GlobalProtect processes running under Dana's account, although neither service is approved by the supplied environment context.",
      "claim_type": "observed_fact",
      "record_ids": ["S07-00299", "S07-00305"]
    }
  ],
  "known_telemetry_limitations": [
    "The available Sysmon query for WS-KORTEGA-01 returned no events, so endpoint process activity there could not be corroborated.",
    "No FILE-LV-01 Windows security events were returned for the reviewed interval.",
    "The proxy query for PROXY-LV-01 returned no events; endpoint proxy records show Windows Update activity but do not explain the 14:15 authentication from the proxy address.",
    "No Zeek TLS records were returned for Dana's workstation in the interval, and its DNS records show only domain-controller lookups; these results do not establish the absence of other communications."
  ],
  "claims_not_established": [
    "The evidence does not establish how Dana's credentials were used from the proxy address or whether this resulted from compromise, misconfiguration, or another cause.",
    "The evidence does not establish that the PowerShell patch script or update package was malicious; the observed command and network activity are consistent with the documented patch procedure.",
    "The evidence does not establish whether Google Drive File Stream or GlobalProtect communicated externally, or whether either process was related to the unusual authentication.",
    "The evidence does not establish the contents, integrity, or outcome of the patch script and update package."
  ],
  "recommended_action": "escalate",
  "additional_evidence_needed": [
    "Investigate the source of the 14:15 authentication from 10.20.20.30, including proxy, network, and authentication infrastructure logs, and verify whether that source address can legitimately originate domain authentication.",
    "Review WS-KORTEGA-01 endpoint telemetry and interactive-session records around 14:15 UTC, including the process and session associated with the successful Dana logon.",
    "Obtain endpoint security, file, and process telemetry for Dana's workstation covering Google Drive File Stream and GlobalProtect, and verify their installation, authorization, and network activity.",
    "Verify the patch script, downloaded update package, and patch execution against approved IT change records and known-good artifacts."
  ]
}
